        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Left lower leg ulcer"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Patient reports chronic ulcer on and off for years, with this episode lasting approximately 4–5 months. Approximately 3 x 4 cm shallow ulcer at the medial gaiter, with irregular sloping edges, granulation tissue and some yellow slough. Moderate serous ooze. No foul smell. Mild erythema and warmth limited to a 0.5–1 cm rim; no clear spreading redness, crepitus or necrosis. Chronic venous skin changes including haemosiderin, mild lipodermatosclerosis and varicosities."
      }
    },
